{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":203,"recorded_at":1780531400000401,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6c-51ee-77b0-8c0a-83cd0025c085"},"task_id":"01a0ad6c-51ee-77b0-8c0a-83cd0025c085","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6c-51ee-77b0-8c0a-83cd0025c085","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(5282 line(s) above)\n5283|### 10.5 Materialization Plan\n5284|\n5285|Materialization Plan schema\n5286|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-plan</code> version <code>1.0.0</code> is\n5287|immutable and authorizes only the exact staged changes it lists. It is not an\n5288|ownership grant.\n5289|\n5290|Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n5291|\n5292|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5293|| --- | --- | --- |\n5294|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Plan schema identifier |\n5295|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n5296|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n5297|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>workspace</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>task_board</code>, or <code>composite</code> |\n5298|| <code>intent</code> | enum | <code>passive_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n5299|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Logical session for provider/task-board/composite; Workspace Group for workspace-only |\n5300|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated immutable recovery base |\n5301|| <code>source_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[1..1024] | Complete source-checkpoint manifest/bundle inputs |\n5302|| <code>derived_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..1024] | Empty except for exact fork projections |\n5303|| <code>fork_projection</code> | Fork Workspace Projection or null | Non-null exactly for <code>intent = fork</code> |\n5304|| <code>prepared_for_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Only this allowlisted host may execute the plan |\n5305|| <code>source_lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero; exact source checkpoint lease |\n5306|| <code>source_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Exact source checkpoint fencing token |\n5307|| <code>authorities</code> | RootAuthority[0..512] | Empty only for the provider backend-identity validation-only variant; otherwise closed destination-local roots defined below |\n5308|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only when destination is classified absent or empty |\n5309|| <code>operations</code> | PlanOperation[0..65536] | Consecutive sequence beginning at 1 when non-empty |\n5310|| <code>exclusions</code> | sorted unique exclusion-class[0..128] | Exact capture/materialization policy classes |\n5311|| <code>validations</code> | sorted unique validation-name[1..6] | Required pre-commit checks from the closed registry below |\n5312|| <code>commit_strategy</code> | enum | <code>validation_only</code>, <code>atomic_directory_rename</code>, <code>atomic_file_merge</code>, <code>single_root_transaction</code>, or <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5313|| <code>rollback_required</code> | boolean | MUST be true in 1.0.0 |\n5314|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Plan author; normally destination host |\n5315|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n5316|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n5317|\n5318|<code>RootAuthority</code> is a closed tagged union, sorted by\n5319|<code>authority_id</code>. IDs use the Section 7.5 <code>root-id</code> grammar,\n5320|are unique in the plan, and are routing labels rather than cross-host\n5321|identities:\n5322|\n5323|| Tag | Exact members |\n5324|| --- | --- |\n5325|| <code>kind = workspace</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:workspace</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>logical_root:string[1..64]</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>write_policy:managed_replace&#124;managed_copy&#124;managed_worktree</code> |\n5326|| <code>kind = provider_store</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:provider_store</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>write_policy:managed_merge</code> |\n5327|| <code>kind = task_board_staging</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:task_board_staging</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>bridge_protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>staging_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>write_policy:staged_install</code> |\n5328|\n5329|A workspace authority's logical root MUST exist in destination configuration,\n5330|its root path MUST equal that resolved mapping, and its group ID MUST equal the\n5331|referenced workspace manifest. A provider-store authority is valid only when\n5332|returned by the exact destination adapter's materialize plan and independently\n5333|accepted by the Section 7.5 root/exclusion checks. A task-board staging root\n5334|MUST be a fresh owner-only child of the resolved ax state root and MUST contain\n5335|no pre-existing manager state. Authorities MUST be pairwise path-disjoint;\n5336|neither a symlink nor a reparse point may make them overlap. Ax data, cache,\n5337|runtime, credential, authentication, SSH, and live manager roots are forbidden\n5338|except for the exact fresh task-board staging child.\n5339|\n5340|<code>ForkWorkspaceProjection</code> is a closed object containing exactly:\n5341|\n5342|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5343|| --- | --- | --- |\n5344|| <code>projection_version</code> | enum | Literal <code>workspace_fork_v1</code> |\n5345|| <code>source_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Session whose checkpoint is the immutable source |\n5346|| <code>source_workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Source group named by the checkpoint closure |\n5347|| <code>source_workspace_group_record_id</code> | digest | Exact source topology record |\n5348|| <code>source_workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Exact source workspace-group Transfer Manifest |\n5349|| <code>destination_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Newly allocated fork session |\n5350|| <code>destination_workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Fresh group identity |\n5351|| <code>destination_workspace_group_record_id</code> | digest | Exact derived Workspace Group Record identity |\n5352|| <code>destination_display_name</code> | string[1..128] | New topology display name |\n5353|| <code>destination_created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Destination record author |\n5354|| <code>destination_created_at</code> | timestamp | Destination record creation time |\n5355|| <code>destination_extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS Workspace Group Record extensions |\n5356|| <code>member_mappings</code> | ForkMemberMapping[1..256] | Sorted by source workspace ID; one-to-one and onto destination members |\n5357|| <code>manifest_mappings</code> | ForkManifestMapping[1..1024] | Sorted by source manifest ID; complete bottom-up re-identification map |\n5358|\n5359|<code>ForkMemberMapping</code> contains exactly\n5360|<code>source_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n5361|<code>destination_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n5362|<code>group_relative_path:path</code>. The relative path MUST equal the path in\n5363|both topology records; every destination ID is fresh and unique. The complete\n5364|destination Workspace Group Record is constructed with the fixed schema and\n5365|version, record/subject/group IDs from these projection fields, the displayed\n5366|name/creation/extensions fields, and the source record's member objects in\n5367|source workspace-ID order after replacing only each workspace ID according to\n5368|<code>member_mappings</code>. Its recomputed record ID MUST equal\n5369|<code>destination_workspace_group_record_id</code> before persistence.\n5370|<code>ForkManifestMapping</code> contains exactly\n5371|<code>kind:workspace_group|workspace_tree</code>,\n5372|<code>source_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n5373|<code>destination_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n5374|<code>source_subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n5375|<code>destination_subject_id:UUIDv7</code>. Ax derives a destination manifest\n5376|by copying every non-identity field, entry, descriptor, and blob reference from\n5377|the source; replacing the subject, group, member, and child-manifest identities\n5378|according to the two maps; and recomputing child identities before parent\n5379|identities. It MUST persist the destination topology and all destination\n5380|manifests before publishing the fork Session Record. Source objects and bytes\n5381|remain unchanged. <code>derived_manifest_ids</code> MUST equal exactly the\n5382|destination IDs in <code>manifest_mappings</code> and MUST NOT occur in\n5383|<code>source_manifest_ids</code>.\n5384|\n5385|The following table is the complete major-v1 plan-kind tagged-union contract.\n5386|Anything not explicitly allowed in its row is forbidden:\n5387|\n5388|| <code>kind</code> | Subject and source inputs | Required authority/action set | Required validations | Legal commit strategies |\n5389|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n5390|| <code>workspace</code> | Subject is the destination Workspace Group. Exactly one workspace-group Transfer Manifest, plus its closed child manifests, is selected from <code>source_manifest_ids</code> or, for a fork, <code>derived_manifest_ids</code>. | One or more <code>workspace</code> authorities; only <code>install_workspace_group</code>, <code>install_workspace_tree</code>, <code>delete_managed_path</code>, or <code>replace_managed_replica</code>. At least one install operation is required. | Exactly <code>manifest_closure</code> and <code>workspace_state</code> | <code>atomic_directory_rename</code> for one directory boundary; <code>atomic_file_merge</code> for one authority with file boundaries only; otherwise <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5391|| <code>provider</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one provider Transfer Manifest is selected. A backend-resolved provider with <code>portable_store=false</code> uses the required zero-entry provider manifest that references its Provider Identity Record. | For a portable store, one or more <code>provider_store</code> authorities and only <code>merge_provider_store</code>. For a backend-resolved identity, no authorities and no operations. | <code>manifest_closure</code> plus exactly one of <code>provider_native_discovery</code> or <code>backend_identity</code> | <code>validation_only</code> only for the zero-operation backend path; <code>atomic_file_merge</code> for file boundaries; <code>single_root_transaction</code> for one provider-store authority with any directory boundary; otherwise <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5392|| <code>task_board</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one Task-board Bundle is selected. | Exactly one <code>task_board_staging</code> authority and exactly one <code>install_task_board_bundle</code> operation at <code>authority_root</code>. | <code>manifest_closure</code>, <code>task_board_bundle</code>, and <code>task_board_validate</code> exactly when the projected board kind is <code>local</code> | <code>single_root_transaction</code> |\n5393|| <code>composite</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one workspace-group manifest and exactly one provider manifest or Task-board Bundle are selected; never both provider and task-board branches. Fork-derived workspace manifests are allowed only with <code>intent=fork</code>. | The disjoint union of the corresponding workspace row and exactly one provider or task-board row. | Exact union of the component rows | <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> when both components mutate; when the provider component is <code>validation_only</code>, use the workspace row's one-root strategy because only workspace bytes mutate |\n5394|\n5395|<code>intent=fork</code> requires non-null <code>fork_projection</code> and a\n5396|non-empty <code>derived_manifest_ids</code>; every other intent requires null\n5397|and an empty array. For a fork plan, <code>subject_id</code> is the destination\n5398|session for provider, task-board, or composite kinds and is the destination\n5399|group for workspace kind. A plan MUST reject a source ID that is not in the\n5400|validated checkpoint closure, a derived ID that is not produced by the exact\n5401|projection, or an authority/action/validation/strategy combination outside its\n5402|row.\n5403|\n5404|Despite the historical member name, <code>source_manifest_ids</code> contains\n5405|Task-board Bundle IDs directly in the task-board row; it never contains raw\n5406|blob IDs, Provider Identity Record IDs, or Materialization Plan IDs. The kind\n5407|row and Checkpoint field determine each ID's schema unambiguously.\n5408|\n5409|~~~json\n5410|{\n5411|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-plan\",\n5412|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n5413|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5414|  \"kind\": \"composite\",\n5415|  \"intent\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n5416|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n5417|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n5418|  \"source_manifest_ids\": [\n5419|    \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n5420|    \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\"\n5421|  ],\n5422|  \"derived_manifest_ids\": [],\n5423|  \"fork_projection\": null,\n5424|  \"prepared_for_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n5425|  \"source_lease_epoch\": 4,\n5426|  \"source_lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n5427|  \"authorities\": [\n5428|    {\n5429|      \"authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n5430|      \"kind\": \"provider_store\",\n5431|      \"platform\": \"linux\",\n5432|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\",\n5433|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n5434|      \"root_role\": \"durable_store\",\n5435|      \"write_policy\": \"managed_merge\"\n5436|    },\n5437|    {\n5438|      \"authority_id\": \"workspace_relux\",\n5439|      \"kind\": \"workspace\",\n5440|      \"platform\": \"linux\",\n5441|      \"root_path\": \"/srv/relux\",\n5442|      \"logical_root\": \"relux\",\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":204,"recorded_at":1780531400000403,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6c-51ee-77b0-8c0a-83cd0025c085"},"task_id":"01a0ad6c-51ee-77b0-8c0a-83cd0025c085","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ad6c-51ee-77b0-8c0a-83cd0025c085"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":205,"recorded_at":1780531400000405,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6c-522d-7da0-8792-62fe2fe7b2cf"},"task_id":"01a0ad6c-522d-7da0-8792-62fe2fe7b2cf","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6c-522d-7da0-8792-62fe2fe7b2cf","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(5727 line(s) above)\n5728|### 10.6 Materialization Journal\n5729|\n5730|Materialization Journal schema\n5731|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal</code> version\n5732|<code>2.0.0</code> is a two-variant machine-local recovery contract. Both the\n5733|mutable journal and immutable managed-replica marker MUST NOT be replicated.\n5734|The journal top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n5735|\n5736|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5737|| --- | --- | --- |\n5738|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n5739|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n5740|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>journal</code> |\n5741|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable across retries |\n5742|| <code>prepare_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Caller-stable Mesh RPC prepare idempotency key, allocated with the materialization ID before the first request |\n5743|| <code>prepare_request_digest</code> | digest | SHA-256 of the complete canonical <code>materialize.prepare</code> request body, including both caller-stable IDs |\n5744|| <code>transfer_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Null when all inputs already exist locally |\n5745|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Exact Materialization Plan |\n5746|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated source checkpoint |\n5747|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Non-null when workspace bytes participate |\n5748|| <code>authority_states</code> | map(root-id,Authority Journal State)[0..512] | Exactly one entry per plan RootAuthority; empty only for validation-only provider plan |\n5749|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for absent/empty destination |\n5750|| <code>completed_blob_chunks</code> | map(digest,sorted unique uint32[0..32768])[0..65536] | Chunk indexes keyed by their Blob ID; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n5751|| <code>verified_blob_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..65536] | Whole-blob verification, not chunk presence; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n5752|| <code>phase</code> | enum | <code>staging</code>, <code>validating</code>, <code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, <code>rolling_back</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, <code>committed</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5753|| <code>provider_transaction</code> | Provider Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when a provider plugin participates |\n5754|| <code>task_board_transaction</code> | Task-board Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when the task-board bridge participates |\n5755|| <code>destination_marker_id</code> | digest or null | Managed-replica marker; non-null in committed workspace/composite transactions |\n5756|| <code>last_error</code> | Structured Error or null | Redacted exact Section 15.1 object |\n5757|| <code>started_at</code> | timestamp | First durable journal write |\n5758|| <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp | Latest durable transition, not authority |\n5759|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS machine-local extensions only |\n5760|\n5761|Provider Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly\n5762|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n5763|<code>state:unknown|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>,\n5764|<code>rollback_token:base64url-256+|null</code>,\n5765|<code>transaction_authority:ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>, and\n5766|<code>last_status_at:timestamp</code>. Prepared requires a non-null token;\n5767|every other state requires null. The token and transaction root are\n5768|machine-local and MUST be redacted from ordinary logs. The authority's\n5769|materialization, provider, transaction, and plan IDs MUST equal the journal and\n5770|referenced plan; its root is the only path passed to later plugin processes.\n5771|\n5772|Task-board Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly:\n5773|\n5774|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5775|| --- | --- | --- |\n5776|| <code>bundle_id</code> | digest | Exact Task-board Bundle installed by the plan |\n5777|| <code>activation_mode</code> | enum | <code>dormant_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n5778|| <code>import_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge import key allocated before import |\n5779|| <code>open_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge open key allocated before open |\n5780|| <code>adopt_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge adopt key allocated before adopt |\n5781|| <code>resume_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge resume key allocated before resume |\n5782|| <code>state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>imported</code>, <code>opened</code>, <code>adopted</code>, <code>resumed</code>, <code>dormant_finalized</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5783|| <code>import_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n5784|| <code>staged_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n5785|| <code>import_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while import token is usable |\n5786|| <code>open_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null from opened until adopt or dormant finalization |\n5787|| <code>dormant_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null in <code>opened</code> and <code>dormant_finalized</code>; consumed and replaced by <code>manager_session_ref</code> on adopt |\n5788|| <code>open_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while open token is usable |\n5789|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n5790|| <code>ax_binding</code> | Ax Binding or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n5791|| <code>last_bridge_state</code> | enum or null | <code>dormant</code>, <code>quiesced</code>, <code>stopped</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5792|| <code>last_status_at</code> | timestamp or null | Time of last bridge status reconciliation |\n5793|| <code>cleanup_state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>pending_expiry</code>, <code>retained_active</code>, or <code>removed</code> |\n5794|| <code>cleanup_after</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null only for dormant finalized state; copied from the last open expiry |\n5795|\n5796|Ax Binding is the exact closed bridge shape\n5797|<code>{ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4}</code>.\n5798|The four operation IDs are allocated once with the materialization ID and MUST\n5799|survive process restart. A retry MUST use the same operation ID and byte-equal\n5800|body. Tokens and manager references are local recovery capabilities: they MUST\n5801|be encrypted with the platform credential facility when available, owner-only\n5802|at rest otherwise, redacted from ordinary logs, excluded from replication, and\n5803|never returned by Mesh RPC.\n5804|\n5805|The null/state invariants are exact. <code>not_started</code> has all tokens and\n5806|references null. <code>imported</code> has import token, staged reference, and\n5807|import expiry only. <code>opened</code> has open token, dormant reference, and\n5808|open expiry only. <code>adopted</code> and <code>resumed</code> have manager\n5809|reference and binding only; their cleanup state is\n5810|<code>retained_active</code>. <code>dormant_finalized</code> has dormant\n5811|reference only, no usable token, bridge state <code>dormant</code>, and cleanup\n5812|state <code>pending_expiry</code> with non-null <code>cleanup_after</code> equal\n5813|to the consumed open expiry. Every other state requires\n5814|<code>cleanup_after = null</code>. <code>rolled_back</code> has no token or\n5815|reference and cleanup state <code>removed</code>. <code>failed</code> preserves\n5816|only the still-valid token/reference pair needed for deterministic status or\n5817|expiry recovery; <code>last_error</code> explains the failure.\n5818|\n5819|Authority Journal State is a closed object containing exactly\n5820|<code>root_path:absolute-path</code>,\n5821|<code>completed_sequences:sorted unique uint53[0..65536]</code>,\n5822|<code>observed_prior_digest:digest|null</code>,\n5823|<code>rollback_root:absolute-path|null</code>, and\n5824|<code>state:staging|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>. The root path MUST\n5825|equal its plan authority; completed sequences contain only operations naming\n5826|that authority. Prepared requires a non-null rollback root, committed and\n5827|rolled-back require null after cleanup, and staging permits null only before\n5828|the first target backup exists. The observed prior digest equals every\n5829|non-null operation predecessor for a one-target authority; an authority with\n5830|multiple distinct predecessors uses null here and each operation backup stores\n5831|its own digest under the rollback root. For a provider-store authority, the\n5832|rollback root MUST equal\n5833|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path/backups/&lt;authority-id&gt;</code>;\n5834|the host journal references the plugin backup and MUST NOT allocate a second\n5835|provider backup location.\n5836|\n5837|After a crash, <code>ax</code> MUST resume a valid staging transaction or roll\n5838|it back. It MUST NOT guess whether an incomplete commit succeeded; it MUST\n5839|reconcile the journal, destination marker, and manifest digest.\n5840|\n5841|Normative example:\n5842|\n5843|~~~json\n5844|{\n5845|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal\",\n5846|  \"schema_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n5847|  \"document_kind\": \"journal\",\n5848|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n5849|  \"prepare_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-b180-72cc-9271-1234567890ab\",\n5850|  \"prepare_request_digest\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\n5851|  \"transfer_id\": \"0198f4c8-d3a0-74bb-9475-1234567890ab\",\n5852|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5853|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n5854|  \"managed_replica_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\n5855|  \"authority_states\": {\n5856|    \"codex_sessions\": {\n5857|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\",\n5858|      \"completed_sequences\": [2],\n5859|      \"observed_prior_digest\": null,\n5860|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab/backups/codex_sessions\",\n5861|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n5862|    },\n5863|    \"workspace_relux\": {\n5864|      \"root_path\": \"/srv/relux\",\n5865|      \"completed_sequences\": [1],\n5866|      \"observed_prior_digest\": \"sha256:3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333\",\n5867|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/materializations/0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab/workspace_relux\",\n5868|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n5869|    }\n5870|  },\n5871|  \"expected_prior_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n5872|  \"completed_blob_chunks\": {\n5873|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\": [0],\n5874|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\": [0]\n5875|  },\n5876|  \"verified_blob_ids\": [\n5877|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\",\n5878|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\"\n5879|  ],\n5880|  \"phase\": \"prepared\",\n5881|  \"provider_transaction\": {\n5882|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n5883|    \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5884|    \"state\": \"prepared\",\n5885|    \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n5886|    \"transaction_authority\": {\n5887|      \"authority_id\": \"provider_transaction\",\n5888|      \"kind\": \"provider_transaction\",\n5889|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5890|      \"layout\": \"provider_transaction_v1\",\n5891|      \"access\": \"read_write\",\n5892|      \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n5893|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n5894|      \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5895|      \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5896|      \"same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids\": [\"codex_sessions\"]\n5897|    },\n5898|    \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\"\n5899|  },\n5900|  \"task_board_transaction\": null,\n5901|  \"destination_marker_id\": null,\n5902|  \"last_error\": null,\n5903|  \"started_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:00.000Z\",\n5904|  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n5905|  \"extensions\": {}\n5906|}\n5907|~~~\n5908|\n5909|The two map members above are the normative\n5910|<code>MJ-MULTIBLOB-POS</code> fixture: chunk zero for two different blobs is two\n5911|independent facts. A flat <code>[0]</code> list is not a valid journal shape.\n5912|Crash recovery fixtures are:\n5913|\n5914|| Fixture | Durable facts after restart | Required recovery |\n5915|| --- | --- | --- |\n5916|| <code>MJ-CRASH-STAGE</code> | Some per-blob chunk sets, no verified whole blob | Request only absent indexes; never mark another blob's equal index present |\n5917|| <code>MJ-RPC-PREPARE-LOST</code> | The destination journal and prepare receipt exist, but the Mesh RPC response was lost | Retry <code>materialize.prepare</code> with the caller-retained operation/materialization IDs and identical body; return the recorded result and create no second journal, authority, replica, plan, or bridge ID |\n5918|| <code>MJ-CRASH-PREPARE-LOST</code> | Provider call may have prepared but response was lost | Call <code>materialize-status</code> with the same IDs; persist returned prepared token before any commit/rollback |\n5919|| <code>MJ-CRASH-COMMIT-LOST</code> | Journal says committing | Status <code>committed</code> plus exact destination marker commits the journal; prepared rolls back or retries commit; unknown fails closed |\n5920|| <code>MJ-CRASH-ROLLBACK-LOST</code> | Journal says rolling_back | Status <code>rolled_back</code> plus restored predecessor closes recovery; prepared retries rollback; unknown fails closed |\n5921|| <code>MJ-CRASH-MARKER-MISMATCH</code> | Plugin says committed but destination marker/plan differs | <code>integrity_failure</code>; quarantine transaction and mutate nothing further |\n5922|\n5923|The following embedded value is the normative\n5924|<code>MJ-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-POS</code> fixture. It is persisted in\n5925|<code>task_board_transaction</code> before <code>materialize.commit</code>\n5926|returns <code>prepared</code>:\n5927|\n5928|~~~json\n5929|{\n5930|  \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n5931|  \"activation_mode\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n5932|  \"import_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a10-71aa-8111-1234567890ab\",\n5933|  \"open_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a20-72bb-8222-1234567890ab\",\n5934|  \"adopt_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a30-73cc-8333-1234567890ab\",\n5935|  \"resume_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a40-74dd-8444-1234567890ab\",\n5936|  \"state\": \"opened\",\n5937|  \"import_token\": null,\n5938|  \"staged_manager_ref\": null,\n5939|  \"import_expires_at\": null,\n5940|  \"open_token\": \"b3duZXItb25seS1vcGVuLXRva2VuLTAxMjM0NTY3ODlhYmNkZWY\",\n5941|  \"dormant_manager_ref\": \"tbm:dormant:0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n5942|  \"open_expires_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:22:10.000Z\",\n5943|  \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n5944|  \"ax_binding\": null,\n5945|  \"last_bridge_state\": \"dormant\",\n5946|  \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n5947|  \"cleanup_state\": \"not_started\",\n5948|  \"cleanup_after\": null\n5949|}\n5950|~~~\n5951|\n5952|Task-board staging is part of the materialization transaction, not a\n5953|precondition performed outside it. The coordinator MUST follow this order for\n5954|graceful takeover, force takeover, passive sync, owner resume, and fork:\n5955|\n5956|1. Before the first call, the caller allocates the materialization and prepare\n5957|   operation IDs. <code>materialize.prepare</code> creates the journal by durably\n5958|   binding both IDs and the canonical request digest before allocating a fresh\n5959|   staging authority or four stable bridge operation IDs and before any bridge\n5960|   mutation.\n5961|2. Transfer installs and validates the bundle at that authority. The\n5962|   coordinator calls bridge <code>import</code>, persists the imported state,\n5963|   calls <code>open</code>, and persists the opened state. A passive replica\n5964|   stops here; owner activation is forbidden before the applicable lease is\n5965|   authoritative.\n5966|3. <code>materialize.commit</code> installs all non-task-board authorities and\n5967|   returns <code>prepared</code> only after the opened state is durable. A\n5968|   task-board-only transaction still uses this commit phase and\n5969|   <code>single_root_transaction</code>.\n5970|4. For <code>dormant_replica</code>, finalize securely destroys ax's local copy\n5971|   of the open token, records <code>dormant_finalized</code>, and leaves the\n5972|   manager inert until the bridge's mandatory token/dormant-state expiry; v1\n5973|   defines no unlisted bridge invalidation operation. For an owner path, finalize verifies\n5974|   the destination lease, calls <code>adopt</code> with the persisted token and\n5975|   exact Ax Binding, verifies bridge status, calls <code>resume</code> with the\n5976|   persisted profile, verifies running/idle, and only then records\n5977|   <code>resumed</code> and commits cleanup.\n5978|5. Before successful adopt, rollback uses the stable IDs to query status,\n5979|   invalidates or lets expire the staged/dormant state, removes the fresh\n5980|   staging authority, and restores every other authority. After successful\n5981|   adopt, the manager is active authority: byte rollback is forbidden; recovery\n5982|   must fence/stop that manager or finish resume/finalize under the same lease.\n5983|\n5984|Bridge status plus the journal is the only recovery authority. The following\n5985|cases are mandatory:\n5986|\n5987|| Fixture | Crash/lost response | Recovery |\n5988|| --- | --- | --- |\n5989|| <code>TB-TXN-IMPORT-LOST</code> | Import may have succeeded; journal is <code>not_started</code> | Retry import with identical operation ID/body; persist the returned identical token/reference or reject <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> |\n5990|| <code>TB-TXN-OPEN-LOST</code> | Open may have succeeded; imported facts are durable | Retry open with its stable ID; bridge returns the same dormant reference/token; persist before commit |\n5991|| <code>TB-TXN-ADOPT-LOST</code> | Adopt may have succeeded after the lease became authoritative | Query bridge status by dormant/manager reference and exact binding, then retry adopt with the same ID; never import a second manager |\n5992|| <code>TB-TXN-RESUME-LOST</code> | Resume may have started provider work | Query status, retry resume only with the same ID/profile, and publish <code>session.resumed</code> once |\n5993|| <code>TB-TXN-TOKEN-EXPIRED</code> | Import/open token expired before adopt | Before lease activation, rollback; after lease activation, remain stopped owner and re-run prepare from the same checkpoint with fresh operation IDs |\n5994|| <code>TB-TXN-BINDING-MISMATCH</code> | Bridge reports another session/epoch/lease | <code>lease_conflict</code>; preserve evidence and mutate nothing further |\n5995|| <code>TB-TXN-PASSIVE</code> | Passive sync reaches opened dormant state | Finalize dormant without adopt/resume; managed replica remains non-executable |\n5996|\n5997|No flow may call bridge import or open before the corresponding journal exists,\n5998|reuse a staging root that contains manager state, inspect private manager state,\n5999|or substitute a blank provider session after a missing/expired bundle.\n6000|\n6001|#### Managed Replica Marker document\n6002|\n6003|The second recovery-contract variant is an immutable Managed Replica Marker.\n6004|It is the authority for classifying a destination as managed; a SQLite row,\n6005|directory name, or prior command success without this marker is not authority.\n6006|Its closed object contains exactly:\n6007|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":206,"recorded_at":1780531400000407,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6c-522d-7da0-8792-62fe2fe7b2cf"},"task_id":"01a0ad6c-522d-7da0-8792-62fe2fe7b2cf","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ad6c-522d-7da0-8792-62fe2fe7b2cf"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":207,"recorded_at":1780531400000409,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"call_id":"call_01a0ad6c4f5f72a3827f5a84f4709aa2","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(5282 line(s) above)\n5283|### 10.5 Materialization Plan\n5284|\n5285|Materialization Plan schema\n5286|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-plan</code> version <code>1.0.0</code> is\n5287|immutable and authorizes only the exact staged changes it lists. It is not an\n5288|ownership grant.\n5289|\n5290|Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n5291|\n5292|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5293|| --- | --- | --- |\n5294|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Plan schema identifier |\n5295|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n5296|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n5297|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>workspace</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>task_board</code>, or <code>composite</code> |\n5298|| <code>intent</code> | enum | <code>passive_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n5299|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Logical session for provider/task-board/composite; Workspace Group for workspace-only |\n5300|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated immutable recovery base |\n5301|| <code>source_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[1..1024] | Complete source-checkpoint manifest/bundle inputs |\n5302|| <code>derived_manifest_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..1024] | Empty except for exact fork projections |\n5303|| <code>fork_projection</code> | Fork Workspace Projection or null | Non-null exactly for <code>intent = fork</code> |\n5304|| <code>prepared_for_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Only this allowlisted host may execute the plan |\n5305|| <code>source_lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero; exact source checkpoint lease |\n5306|| <code>source_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Exact source checkpoint fencing token |\n5307|| <code>authorities</code> | RootAuthority[0..512] | Empty only for the provider backend-identity validation-only variant; otherwise closed destination-local roots defined below |\n5308|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only when destination is classified absent or empty |\n5309|| <code>operations</code> | PlanOperation[0..65536] | Consecutive sequence beginning at 1 when non-empty |\n5310|| <code>exclusions</code> | sorted unique exclusion-class[0..128] | Exact capture/materialization policy classes |\n5311|| <code>validations</code> | sorted unique validation-name[1..6] | Required pre-commit checks from the closed registry below |\n5312|| <code>commit_strategy</code> | enum | <code>validation_only</code>, <code>atomic_directory_rename</code>, <code>atomic_file_merge</code>, <code>single_root_transaction</code>, or <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5313|| <code>rollback_required</code> | boolean | MUST be true in 1.0.0 |\n5314|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Plan author; normally destination host |\n5315|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n5316|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n5317|\n5318|<code>RootAuthority</code> is a closed tagged union, sorted by\n5319|<code>authority_id</code>. IDs use the Section 7.5 <code>root-id</code> grammar,\n5320|are unique in the plan, and are routing labels rather than cross-host\n5321|identities:\n5322|\n5323|| Tag | Exact members |\n5324|| --- | --- |\n5325|| <code>kind = workspace</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:workspace</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>logical_root:string[1..64]</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>write_policy:managed_replace&#124;managed_copy&#124;managed_worktree</code> |\n5326|| <code>kind = provider_store</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:provider_store</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>write_policy:managed_merge</code> |\n5327|| <code>kind = task_board_staging</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>kind:task_board_staging</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>bridge_protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>staging_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>write_policy:staged_install</code> |\n5328|\n5329|A workspace authority's logical root MUST exist in destination configuration,\n5330|its root path MUST equal that resolved mapping, and its group ID MUST equal the\n5331|referenced workspace manifest. A provider-store authority is valid only when\n5332|returned by the exact destination adapter's materialize plan and independently\n5333|accepted by the Section 7.5 root/exclusion checks. A task-board staging root\n5334|MUST be a fresh owner-only child of the resolved ax state root and MUST contain\n5335|no pre-existing manager state. Authorities MUST be pairwise path-disjoint;\n5336|neither a symlink nor a reparse point may make them overlap. Ax data, cache,\n5337|runtime, credential, authentication, SSH, and live manager roots are forbidden\n5338|except for the exact fresh task-board staging child.\n5339|\n5340|<code>ForkWorkspaceProjection</code> is a closed object containing exactly:\n5341|\n5342|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5343|| --- | --- | --- |\n5344|| <code>projection_version</code> | enum | Literal <code>workspace_fork_v1</code> |\n5345|| <code>source_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Session whose checkpoint is the immutable source |\n5346|| <code>source_workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Source group named by the checkpoint closure |\n5347|| <code>source_workspace_group_record_id</code> | digest | Exact source topology record |\n5348|| <code>source_workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Exact source workspace-group Transfer Manifest |\n5349|| <code>destination_session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Newly allocated fork session |\n5350|| <code>destination_workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Fresh group identity |\n5351|| <code>destination_workspace_group_record_id</code> | digest | Exact derived Workspace Group Record identity |\n5352|| <code>destination_display_name</code> | string[1..128] | New topology display name |\n5353|| <code>destination_created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Destination record author |\n5354|| <code>destination_created_at</code> | timestamp | Destination record creation time |\n5355|| <code>destination_extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS Workspace Group Record extensions |\n5356|| <code>member_mappings</code> | ForkMemberMapping[1..256] | Sorted by source workspace ID; one-to-one and onto destination members |\n5357|| <code>manifest_mappings</code> | ForkManifestMapping[1..1024] | Sorted by source manifest ID; complete bottom-up re-identification map |\n5358|\n5359|<code>ForkMemberMapping</code> contains exactly\n5360|<code>source_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n5361|<code>destination_workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n5362|<code>group_relative_path:path</code>. The relative path MUST equal the path in\n5363|both topology records; every destination ID is fresh and unique. The complete\n5364|destination Workspace Group Record is constructed with the fixed schema and\n5365|version, record/subject/group IDs from these projection fields, the displayed\n5366|name/creation/extensions fields, and the source record's member objects in\n5367|source workspace-ID order after replacing only each workspace ID according to\n5368|<code>member_mappings</code>. Its recomputed record ID MUST equal\n5369|<code>destination_workspace_group_record_id</code> before persistence.\n5370|<code>ForkManifestMapping</code> contains exactly\n5371|<code>kind:workspace_group|workspace_tree</code>,\n5372|<code>source_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n5373|<code>destination_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n5374|<code>source_subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, and\n5375|<code>destination_subject_id:UUIDv7</code>. Ax derives a destination manifest\n5376|by copying every non-identity field, entry, descriptor, and blob reference from\n5377|the source; replacing the subject, group, member, and child-manifest identities\n5378|according to the two maps; and recomputing child identities before parent\n5379|identities. It MUST persist the destination topology and all destination\n5380|manifests before publishing the fork Session Record. Source objects and bytes\n5381|remain unchanged. <code>derived_manifest_ids</code> MUST equal exactly the\n5382|destination IDs in <code>manifest_mappings</code> and MUST NOT occur in\n5383|<code>source_manifest_ids</code>.\n5384|\n5385|The following table is the complete major-v1 plan-kind tagged-union contract.\n5386|Anything not explicitly allowed in its row is forbidden:\n5387|\n5388|| <code>kind</code> | Subject and source inputs | Required authority/action set | Required validations | Legal commit strategies |\n5389|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n5390|| <code>workspace</code> | Subject is the destination Workspace Group. Exactly one workspace-group Transfer Manifest, plus its closed child manifests, is selected from <code>source_manifest_ids</code> or, for a fork, <code>derived_manifest_ids</code>. | One or more <code>workspace</code> authorities; only <code>install_workspace_group</code>, <code>install_workspace_tree</code>, <code>delete_managed_path</code>, or <code>replace_managed_replica</code>. At least one install operation is required. | Exactly <code>manifest_closure</code> and <code>workspace_state</code> | <code>atomic_directory_rename</code> for one directory boundary; <code>atomic_file_merge</code> for one authority with file boundaries only; otherwise <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5391|| <code>provider</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one provider Transfer Manifest is selected. A backend-resolved provider with <code>portable_store=false</code> uses the required zero-entry provider manifest that references its Provider Identity Record. | For a portable store, one or more <code>provider_store</code> authorities and only <code>merge_provider_store</code>. For a backend-resolved identity, no authorities and no operations. | <code>manifest_closure</code> plus exactly one of <code>provider_native_discovery</code> or <code>backend_identity</code> | <code>validation_only</code> only for the zero-operation backend path; <code>atomic_file_merge</code> for file boundaries; <code>single_root_transaction</code> for one provider-store authority with any directory boundary; otherwise <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> |\n5392|| <code>task_board</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one Task-board Bundle is selected. | Exactly one <code>task_board_staging</code> authority and exactly one <code>install_task_board_bundle</code> operation at <code>authority_root</code>. | <code>manifest_closure</code>, <code>task_board_bundle</code>, and <code>task_board_validate</code> exactly when the projected board kind is <code>local</code> | <code>single_root_transaction</code> |\n5393|| <code>composite</code> | Subject is one Session. Exactly one workspace-group manifest and exactly one provider manifest or Task-board Bundle are selected; never both provider and task-board branches. Fork-derived workspace manifests are allowed only with <code>intent=fork</code>. | The disjoint union of the corresponding workspace row and exactly one provider or task-board row. | Exact union of the component rows | <code>two_phase_multi_root</code> when both components mutate; when the provider component is <code>validation_only</code>, use the workspace row's one-root strategy because only workspace bytes mutate |\n5394|\n5395|<code>intent=fork</code> requires non-null <code>fork_projection</code> and a\n5396|non-empty <code>derived_manifest_ids</code>; every other intent requires null\n5397|and an empty array. For a fork plan, <code>subject_id</code> is the destination\n5398|session for provider, task-board, or composite kinds and is the destination\n5399|group for workspace kind. A plan MUST reject a source ID that is not in the\n5400|validated checkpoint closure, a derived ID that is not produced by the exact\n5401|projection, or an authority/action/validation/strategy combination outside its\n5402|row.\n5403|\n5404|Despite the historical member name, <code>source_manifest_ids</code> contains\n5405|Task-board Bundle IDs directly in the task-board row; it never contains raw\n5406|blob IDs, Provider Identity Record IDs, or Materialization Plan IDs. The kind\n5407|row and Checkpoint field determine each ID's schema unambiguously.\n5408|\n5409|~~~json\n5410|{\n5411|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-plan\",\n5412|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n5413|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5414|  \"kind\": \"composite\",\n5415|  \"intent\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n5416|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n5417|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n5418|  \"source_manifest_ids\": [\n5419|    \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n5420|    \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\"\n5421|  ],\n5422|  \"derived_manifest_ids\": [],\n5423|  \"fork_projection\": null,\n5424|  \"prepared_for_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n5425|  \"source_lease_epoch\": 4,\n5426|  \"source_lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n5427|  \"authorities\": [\n5428|    {\n5429|      \"authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n5430|      \"kind\": \"provider_store\",\n5431|      \"platform\": \"linux\",\n5432|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\",\n5433|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n5434|      \"root_role\": \"durable_store\",\n5435|      \"write_policy\": \"managed_merge\"\n5436|    },\n5437|    {\n5438|      \"authority_id\": \"workspace_relux\",\n5439|      \"kind\": \"workspace\",\n5440|      \"platform\": \"linux\",\n5441|      \"root_path\": \"/srv/relux\",\n5442|      \"logical_root\": \"relux\",\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":208,"recorded_at":1780531400000411,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"call_id":"call_01a0ad6c503471baaccf6fc050a05e4b","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(5727 line(s) above)\n5728|### 10.6 Materialization Journal\n5729|\n5730|Materialization Journal schema\n5731|<code>urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal</code> version\n5732|<code>2.0.0</code> is a two-variant machine-local recovery contract. Both the\n5733|mutable journal and immutable managed-replica marker MUST NOT be replicated.\n5734|The journal top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n5735|\n5736|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5737|| --- | --- | --- |\n5738|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Materialization Journal schema identifier |\n5739|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>2.0.0</code> |\n5740|| <code>document_kind</code> | enum | Literal <code>journal</code> |\n5741|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable across retries |\n5742|| <code>prepare_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Caller-stable Mesh RPC prepare idempotency key, allocated with the materialization ID before the first request |\n5743|| <code>prepare_request_digest</code> | digest | SHA-256 of the complete canonical <code>materialize.prepare</code> request body, including both caller-stable IDs |\n5744|| <code>transfer_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Null when all inputs already exist locally |\n5745|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest | Exact Materialization Plan |\n5746|| <code>source_checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Validated source checkpoint |\n5747|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null | Non-null when workspace bytes participate |\n5748|| <code>authority_states</code> | map(root-id,Authority Journal State)[0..512] | Exactly one entry per plan RootAuthority; empty only for validation-only provider plan |\n5749|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for absent/empty destination |\n5750|| <code>completed_blob_chunks</code> | map(digest,sorted unique uint32[0..32768])[0..65536] | Chunk indexes keyed by their Blob ID; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n5751|| <code>verified_blob_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..65536] | Whole-blob verification, not chunk presence; sufficient for the maximum file/blob cardinality of one committed transfer closure |\n5752|| <code>phase</code> | enum | <code>staging</code>, <code>validating</code>, <code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, <code>rolling_back</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, <code>committed</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5753|| <code>provider_transaction</code> | Provider Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when a provider plugin participates |\n5754|| <code>task_board_transaction</code> | Task-board Journal Transaction or null | Non-null only when the task-board bridge participates |\n5755|| <code>destination_marker_id</code> | digest or null | Managed-replica marker; non-null in committed workspace/composite transactions |\n5756|| <code>last_error</code> | Structured Error or null | Redacted exact Section 15.1 object |\n5757|| <code>started_at</code> | timestamp | First durable journal write |\n5758|| <code>updated_at</code> | timestamp | Latest durable transition, not authority |\n5759|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS machine-local extensions only |\n5760|\n5761|Provider Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly\n5762|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n5763|<code>state:unknown|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>,\n5764|<code>rollback_token:base64url-256+|null</code>,\n5765|<code>transaction_authority:ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>, and\n5766|<code>last_status_at:timestamp</code>. Prepared requires a non-null token;\n5767|every other state requires null. The token and transaction root are\n5768|machine-local and MUST be redacted from ordinary logs. The authority's\n5769|materialization, provider, transaction, and plan IDs MUST equal the journal and\n5770|referenced plan; its root is the only path passed to later plugin processes.\n5771|\n5772|Task-board Journal Transaction is a closed object containing exactly:\n5773|\n5774|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n5775|| --- | --- | --- |\n5776|| <code>bundle_id</code> | digest | Exact Task-board Bundle installed by the plan |\n5777|| <code>activation_mode</code> | enum | <code>dormant_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n5778|| <code>import_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge import key allocated before import |\n5779|| <code>open_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge open key allocated before open |\n5780|| <code>adopt_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge adopt key allocated before adopt |\n5781|| <code>resume_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Stable bridge resume key allocated before resume |\n5782|| <code>state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>imported</code>, <code>opened</code>, <code>adopted</code>, <code>resumed</code>, <code>dormant_finalized</code>, <code>rolled_back</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5783|| <code>import_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n5784|| <code>staged_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null exactly in <code>imported</code> and consumed by <code>open</code> |\n5785|| <code>import_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while import token is usable |\n5786|| <code>open_token</code> | base64url-256+ or null | Owner-only bridge token; non-null from opened until adopt or dormant finalization |\n5787|| <code>dormant_manager_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null in <code>opened</code> and <code>dormant_finalized</code>; consumed and replaced by <code>manager_session_ref</code> on adopt |\n5788|| <code>open_expires_at</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null exactly while open token is usable |\n5789|| <code>manager_session_ref</code> | string[1..512] or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n5790|| <code>ax_binding</code> | Ax Binding or null | Non-null after successful adopt |\n5791|| <code>last_bridge_state</code> | enum or null | <code>dormant</code>, <code>quiesced</code>, <code>stopped</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>, or <code>failed</code> |\n5792|| <code>last_status_at</code> | timestamp or null | Time of last bridge status reconciliation |\n5793|| <code>cleanup_state</code> | enum | <code>not_started</code>, <code>pending_expiry</code>, <code>retained_active</code>, or <code>removed</code> |\n5794|| <code>cleanup_after</code> | timestamp or null | Non-null only for dormant finalized state; copied from the last open expiry |\n5795|\n5796|Ax Binding is the exact closed bridge shape\n5797|<code>{ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4}</code>.\n5798|The four operation IDs are allocated once with the materialization ID and MUST\n5799|survive process restart. A retry MUST use the same operation ID and byte-equal\n5800|body. Tokens and manager references are local recovery capabilities: they MUST\n5801|be encrypted with the platform credential facility when available, owner-only\n5802|at rest otherwise, redacted from ordinary logs, excluded from replication, and\n5803|never returned by Mesh RPC.\n5804|\n5805|The null/state invariants are exact. <code>not_started</code> has all tokens and\n5806|references null. <code>imported</code> has import token, staged reference, and\n5807|import expiry only. <code>opened</code> has open token, dormant reference, and\n5808|open expiry only. <code>adopted</code> and <code>resumed</code> have manager\n5809|reference and binding only; their cleanup state is\n5810|<code>retained_active</code>. <code>dormant_finalized</code> has dormant\n5811|reference only, no usable token, bridge state <code>dormant</code>, and cleanup\n5812|state <code>pending_expiry</code> with non-null <code>cleanup_after</code> equal\n5813|to the consumed open expiry. Every other state requires\n5814|<code>cleanup_after = null</code>. <code>rolled_back</code> has no token or\n5815|reference and cleanup state <code>removed</code>. <code>failed</code> preserves\n5816|only the still-valid token/reference pair needed for deterministic status or\n5817|expiry recovery; <code>last_error</code> explains the failure.\n5818|\n5819|Authority Journal State is a closed object containing exactly\n5820|<code>root_path:absolute-path</code>,\n5821|<code>completed_sequences:sorted unique uint53[0..65536]</code>,\n5822|<code>observed_prior_digest:digest|null</code>,\n5823|<code>rollback_root:absolute-path|null</code>, and\n5824|<code>state:staging|prepared|committed|rolled_back</code>. The root path MUST\n5825|equal its plan authority; completed sequences contain only operations naming\n5826|that authority. Prepared requires a non-null rollback root, committed and\n5827|rolled-back require null after cleanup, and staging permits null only before\n5828|the first target backup exists. The observed prior digest equals every\n5829|non-null operation predecessor for a one-target authority; an authority with\n5830|multiple distinct predecessors uses null here and each operation backup stores\n5831|its own digest under the rollback root. For a provider-store authority, the\n5832|rollback root MUST equal\n5833|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path/backups/&lt;authority-id&gt;</code>;\n5834|the host journal references the plugin backup and MUST NOT allocate a second\n5835|provider backup location.\n5836|\n5837|After a crash, <code>ax</code> MUST resume a valid staging transaction or roll\n5838|it back. It MUST NOT guess whether an incomplete commit succeeded; it MUST\n5839|reconcile the journal, destination marker, and manifest digest.\n5840|\n5841|Normative example:\n5842|\n5843|~~~json\n5844|{\n5845|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:materialization-journal\",\n5846|  \"schema_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n5847|  \"document_kind\": \"journal\",\n5848|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n5849|  \"prepare_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-b180-72cc-9271-1234567890ab\",\n5850|  \"prepare_request_digest\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\n5851|  \"transfer_id\": \"0198f4c8-d3a0-74bb-9475-1234567890ab\",\n5852|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5853|  \"source_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n5854|  \"managed_replica_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-2234567890ab\",\n5855|  \"authority_states\": {\n5856|    \"codex_sessions\": {\n5857|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\",\n5858|      \"completed_sequences\": [2],\n5859|      \"observed_prior_digest\": null,\n5860|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab/backups/codex_sessions\",\n5861|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n5862|    },\n5863|    \"workspace_relux\": {\n5864|      \"root_path\": \"/srv/relux\",\n5865|      \"completed_sequences\": [1],\n5866|      \"observed_prior_digest\": \"sha256:3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333\",\n5867|      \"rollback_root\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/materializations/0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab/workspace_relux\",\n5868|      \"state\": \"prepared\"\n5869|    }\n5870|  },\n5871|  \"expected_prior_checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n5872|  \"completed_blob_chunks\": {\n5873|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\": [0],\n5874|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\": [0]\n5875|  },\n5876|  \"verified_blob_ids\": [\n5877|    \"sha256:0e442b07e3772e8f5622478242ddf5f9f197bbd6a0402cd71471db4081abb291\",\n5878|    \"sha256:444e0fffbd825e9610ff5b199485707a0c895339ae80c15cc8a8aee41b106fda\"\n5879|  ],\n5880|  \"phase\": \"prepared\",\n5881|  \"provider_transaction\": {\n5882|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n5883|    \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5884|    \"state\": \"prepared\",\n5885|    \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n5886|    \"transaction_authority\": {\n5887|      \"authority_id\": \"provider_transaction\",\n5888|      \"kind\": \"provider_transaction\",\n5889|      \"root_path\": \"/home/ivan/.local/state/ax/provider-transactions/codex/0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5890|      \"layout\": \"provider_transaction_v1\",\n5891|      \"access\": \"read_write\",\n5892|      \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n5893|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n5894|      \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n5895|      \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n5896|      \"same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids\": [\"codex_sessions\"]\n5897|    },\n5898|    \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\"\n5899|  },\n5900|  \"task_board_transaction\": null,\n5901|  \"destination_marker_id\": null,\n5902|  \"last_error\": null,\n5903|  \"started_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:00.000Z\",\n5904|  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n5905|  \"extensions\": {}\n5906|}\n5907|~~~\n5908|\n5909|The two map members above are the normative\n5910|<code>MJ-MULTIBLOB-POS</code> fixture: chunk zero for two different blobs is two\n5911|independent facts. A flat <code>[0]</code> list is not a valid journal shape.\n5912|Crash recovery fixtures are:\n5913|\n5914|| Fixture | Durable facts after restart | Required recovery |\n5915|| --- | --- | --- |\n5916|| <code>MJ-CRASH-STAGE</code> | Some per-blob chunk sets, no verified whole blob | Request only absent indexes; never mark another blob's equal index present |\n5917|| <code>MJ-RPC-PREPARE-LOST</code> | The destination journal and prepare receipt exist, but the Mesh RPC response was lost | Retry <code>materialize.prepare</code> with the caller-retained operation/materialization IDs and identical body; return the recorded result and create no second journal, authority, replica, plan, or bridge ID |\n5918|| <code>MJ-CRASH-PREPARE-LOST</code> | Provider call may have prepared but response was lost | Call <code>materialize-status</code> with the same IDs; persist returned prepared token before any commit/rollback |\n5919|| <code>MJ-CRASH-COMMIT-LOST</code> | Journal says committing | Status <code>committed</code> plus exact destination marker commits the journal; prepared rolls back or retries commit; unknown fails closed |\n5920|| <code>MJ-CRASH-ROLLBACK-LOST</code> | Journal says rolling_back | Status <code>rolled_back</code> plus restored predecessor closes recovery; prepared retries rollback; unknown fails closed |\n5921|| <code>MJ-CRASH-MARKER-MISMATCH</code> | Plugin says committed but destination marker/plan differs | <code>integrity_failure</code>; quarantine transaction and mutate nothing further |\n5922|\n5923|The following embedded value is the normative\n5924|<code>MJ-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-POS</code> fixture. It is persisted in\n5925|<code>task_board_transaction</code> before <code>materialize.commit</code>\n5926|returns <code>prepared</code>:\n5927|\n5928|~~~json\n5929|{\n5930|  \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n5931|  \"activation_mode\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n5932|  \"import_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a10-71aa-8111-1234567890ab\",\n5933|  \"open_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a20-72bb-8222-1234567890ab\",\n5934|  \"adopt_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a30-73cc-8333-1234567890ab\",\n5935|  \"resume_operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0a40-74dd-8444-1234567890ab\",\n5936|  \"state\": \"opened\",\n5937|  \"import_token\": null,\n5938|  \"staged_manager_ref\": null,\n5939|  \"import_expires_at\": null,\n5940|  \"open_token\": \"b3duZXItb25seS1vcGVuLXRva2VuLTAxMjM0NTY3ODlhYmNkZWY\",\n5941|  \"dormant_manager_ref\": \"tbm:dormant:0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n5942|  \"open_expires_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:22:10.000Z\",\n5943|  \"manager_session_ref\": null,\n5944|  \"ax_binding\": null,\n5945|  \"last_bridge_state\": \"dormant\",\n5946|  \"last_status_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:12:10.000Z\",\n5947|  \"cleanup_state\": \"not_started\",\n5948|  \"cleanup_after\": null\n5949|}\n5950|~~~\n5951|\n5952|Task-board staging is part of the materialization transaction, not a\n5953|precondition performed outside it. The coordinator MUST follow this order for\n5954|graceful takeover, force takeover, passive sync, owner resume, and fork:\n5955|\n5956|1. Before the first call, the caller allocates the materialization and prepare\n5957|   operation IDs. <code>materialize.prepare</code> creates the journal by durably\n5958|   binding both IDs and the canonical request digest before allocating a fresh\n5959|   staging authority or four stable bridge operation IDs and before any bridge\n5960|   mutation.\n5961|2. Transfer installs and validates the bundle at that authority. The\n5962|   coordinator calls bridge <code>import</code>, persists the imported state,\n5963|   calls <code>open</code>, and persists the opened state. A passive replica\n5964|   stops here; owner activation is forbidden before the applicable lease is\n5965|   authoritative.\n5966|3. <code>materialize.commit</code> installs all non-task-board authorities and\n5967|   returns <code>prepared</code> only after the opened state is durable. A\n5968|   task-board-only transaction still uses this commit phase and\n5969|   <code>single_root_transaction</code>.\n5970|4. For <code>dormant_replica</code>, finalize securely destroys ax's local copy\n5971|   of the open token, records <code>dormant_finalized</code>, and leaves the\n5972|   manager inert until the bridge's mandatory token/dormant-state expiry; v1\n5973|   defines no unlisted bridge invalidation operation. For an owner path, finalize verifies\n5974|   the destination lease, calls <code>adopt</code> with the persisted token and\n5975|   exact Ax Binding, verifies bridge status, calls <code>resume</code> with the\n5976|   persisted profile, verifies running/idle, and only then records\n5977|   <code>resumed</code> and commits cleanup.\n5978|5. Before successful adopt, rollback uses the stable IDs to query status,\n5979|   invalidates or lets expire the staged/dormant state, removes the fresh\n5980|   staging authority, and restores every other authority. After successful\n5981|   adopt, the manager is active authority: byte rollback is forbidden; recovery\n5982|   must fence/stop that manager or finish resume/finalize under the same lease.\n5983|\n5984|Bridge status plus the journal is the only recovery authority. The following\n5985|cases are mandatory:\n5986|\n5987|| Fixture | Crash/lost response | Recovery |\n5988|| --- | --- | --- |\n5989|| <code>TB-TXN-IMPORT-LOST</code> | Import may have succeeded; journal is <code>not_started</code> | Retry import with identical operation ID/body; persist the returned identical token/reference or reject <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> |\n5990|| <code>TB-TXN-OPEN-LOST</code> | Open may have succeeded; imported facts are durable | Retry open with its stable ID; bridge returns the same dormant reference/token; persist before commit |\n5991|| <code>TB-TXN-ADOPT-LOST</code> | Adopt may have succeeded after the lease became authoritative | Query bridge status by dormant/manager reference and exact binding, then retry adopt with the same ID; never import a second manager |\n5992|| <code>TB-TXN-RESUME-LOST</code> | Resume may have started provider work | Query status, retry resume only with the same ID/profile, and publish <code>session.resumed</code> once |\n5993|| <code>TB-TXN-TOKEN-EXPIRED</code> | Import/open token expired before adopt | Before lease activation, rollback; after lease activation, remain stopped owner and re-run prepare from the same checkpoint with fresh operation IDs |\n5994|| <code>TB-TXN-BINDING-MISMATCH</code> | Bridge reports another session/epoch/lease | <code>lease_conflict</code>; preserve evidence and mutate nothing further |\n5995|| <code>TB-TXN-PASSIVE</code> | Passive sync reaches opened dormant state | Finalize dormant without adopt/resume; managed replica remains non-executable |\n5996|\n5997|No flow may call bridge import or open before the corresponding journal exists,\n5998|reuse a staging root that contains manager state, inspect private manager state,\n5999|or substitute a blank provider session after a missing/expired bundle.\n6000|\n6001|#### Managed Replica Marker document\n6002|\n6003|The second recovery-contract variant is an immutable Managed Replica Marker.\n6004|It is the authority for classifying a destination as managed; a SQLite row,\n6005|directory name, or prior command success without this marker is not authority.\n6006|Its closed object contains exactly:\n6007|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
