{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c547","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":254,"recorded_at":1780531400000503,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6c-64d4-7de3-89ed-fa052ec70fea"},"task_id":"01a0ad6c-64d4-7de3-89ed-fa052ec70fea","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6c-64d4-7de3-89ed-fa052ec70fea","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessrepo/checkpoint.go`.\n1|// Checkpoint Record attestation for the session-persistence leaf.\n2|//\n3|// Checkpoint Records (urn:ax:schema:checkpoint) are session-persistence\n4|// objects alongside Session Records, Session Events, and Lease Records.\n5|// This helper owns their canonical identity attestation through the\n6|// canonicaljson owner, so query-layer admission (internal/sessquery)\n7|// never attests the binding itself: it calls AttestCheckpointRecord\n8|// and then extracts the already validated members. The provhost\n9|// identity bound allowlists this site with the session record/event\n10|// sites and the lease site.\n11|package sessrepo\n12|\n13|import (\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n16|)\n17|\n18|// AttestCheckpointRecord validates one canonical Checkpoint Record\n19|// frame through the canonicaljson owner and returns its canonical\n20|// digest with the self-identity field. Closed-shape and self-identity\n21|// failures are returned for the caller to map to its refusal class.\n22|func AttestCheckpointRecord(raw []byte) (scalar.Digest, canonicaljson.SelfField, error) {\n23|\treturn canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity(raw)\n24|}","final_result":true}}}
