{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":561,"recorded_at":1780531400001117,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ad6d-12f2-7c00-ab17-e593267d2ed6"},"task_id":"01a0ad6d-12f2-7c00-ab17-e593267d2ed6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ad6d-12f2-7c00-ab17-e593267d2ed6","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-17-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-3k3e6m) { id name status description scope ac }' 2>&1 | head -n 20\\necho ===\\ntask-board q 'get(TASK-260830-17ootk) { id name status description scope ac }' 2>&1 | head -n 20\\necho ===\\ntask-board grep \\\"3qrfjp\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Check sibling tasks and referenced task\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ac\\\":\\\"Production behavior demonstrates: Persist operation receipts, phase transitions, idempotency input digests, status-first recovery, and parked/rollback outcomes. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Persist operation receipts, phase transitions, idempotency input digests, status-first recovery, and parked/rollback outcomes. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-3k3e6m\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"implement-durable-operation-journal\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); §5.4, §10.5-10.6, §13.12-13.13. Work only inside the workspace-checkpoints-and-operation-journal story boundary.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"to-dev\\\"}\\n===\\n{\\\"ac\\\":\\\"Production behavior demonstrates: Crash after every durable boundary and prove exactly safe_retry, explicit_rollback, or recoverable_parked_state. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Crash after every durable boundary and prove exactly safe_retry, explicit_rollback, or recoverable_parked_state. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-17ootk\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"fault-test-local-crash-boundaries\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); §5.4, §10.5-10.6, §13.12-13.13. Work only inside the workspace-checkpoints-and-operation-journal story boundary.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"to-dev\\\"}\\n===\\n.resources/TASK-260830-14yo67/TASK-260830-14yo67_producer.md:1:Own TASK-260830-14yo67 (implement-workspace-checkpoint-records), first leaf of STORY-260830-2rqigd (workspace-checkpoints-and-operation-journal; siblings 3k3e6m durable operation journal and 17ootk crash-boundary fault tests follow you). Implement Checkpoint Record 1.0.0 capture as production code: a typed checkpoint closure over provider identity, workspace manifests, the task-board bundle, terminal evidence and the source head, with exact closed shapes, digests and event-head binding as the pinned sections 5.4, 10.5-10.6 and 13.12-13.13 require; the records you write must be admissible by the landed consumers (internal/sessrepo AttestCheckpointRecord, internal/sessquery admitCheckpoint: owning lease tuple, creator-holder, persistence variant, event heads at or before the owning lease) — drive those consumers in your tests rather than re-implementing admission; include crash/idempotency evidence for every durable capture (interrupted capture leaves no partial record admitted; re-capture is idempotent; a capture whose inputs moved refuses), negatives for every closed-shape and binding rule, and the same-checkpoint/different-inputs digest distinctions. Replace the task's v0.5.0 scope citations with the pinned v0.6.0 headings of the same sections; TASK-260830-3qrfjp's storage crash boundaries are your durable-write model. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree is provisioned by task-board under .temp/<STORY-ID>/worktree on branch task-board/story/<STORY-ID> forked from the current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED for the handoff snapshot, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if git fetch origin shows that origin/main moved past the workspace base before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-14yo67 and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate source, test, harness and documentation paths (no task-board.config.json, no __pycache__/.pyc, no stray plant files; run Python harnesses with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract: every AC sentence and every gate/refusal is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test or declared a stated bound, reported as a ratio (n of m rows driven, call site named); negatives that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; at least one NARROWING mutant per gate (a token-preserving one where a gate inspects text) executed by a shipped harness on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, subprocess return-code exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control, and NOT_APPLIED / COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE reported outside the numerator; crash/idempotency evidence with real process termination where the operation mutates durable state; a conformance matrix mapping each pinned