{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e6f9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ad6b-d9f3-7b60-a446-cfbe978dc3a0"},"sequence":4567,"recorded_at":1780531400009129,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"47d87e75-54e9-4256-91b6-025175a046f7"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nTASK-260830-14yo67 implements Checkpoint Record 1.0.0 capture as new package `internal/sessckpt`: `Store.Capture` builds the typed closure (provider identity, workspace manifest, task-board bundle, terminal evidence, source head) into the closed record, attests via `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord`, and installs blob-first/receipt-second with no-replace durability; `Store.Admit` routes raw records through the same path; `Store.Get` re-verifies on read. AC coverage is 8 of 8 rows driven through the production entries, with the landed `sessquery` consumer driven on captured bytes (epoch-1 + successor admits, wrong-creator refusal).\n\nEvidence attached: `TASK-260830-14yo67_results.md`, `TASK-260830-14yo67_conformance-matrix.md`, and a real gzip `TASK-260830-14yo67_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (full/race/cover/fuzz/gate logs plus per-plant mutant logs). Mutants: 7 of 7 narrowing killed (including token-preserving `N-evidence-enum`) + 1 survived control, via shipped `mutant_harness.py` on the final source. Crash: hook faults plus a real self-SIGKILL child test. Full suite (27 pkgs), race everywhere, tracecheck, cataloggen-check, cross-compiles, and fuzz all green; candidate left uncommitted (`M LOGBOOK.md` + `?? internal/sessckpt/`), origin/main unmoved.\n\nTwo notes for the reviewer: my own negative test caught a real bug pre-handoff (`Admit` skipped the kind check — fixed with `checkSessionKind` + `default` refusal); and the `section:5.4` registry gap is now stale but intentionally untouched since the registry digest is review-pinned against self-minted claims — refresh is left for review-gated maintenance.","reason":null}}
